# Interface fidelity

A missing design input is filled with the named template in the piece reference. Record it under Assumed. The reply says it was taken automatically, which command changes it, and which command regenerates the piece. An accepted file wins, then the fact in this turn, then the template. Do not invent a palette, copy, accessibility notes, test rows, HEART figures, a decision, or a persona's name or biography.

The task uses an accepted analysis, the task in this turn, or template single-task. The path uses an accepted user flow, the path in this turn, or template linear-three, written in this turn. The mock uses an accepted UI kit, the tokens in this turn, a named preset, or plain. The other presets are dense, material-3, hig, and fluent-2, and they apply only when named.

Consistency without a product UI kit (an accepted kit, or tokens in this turn) writes nothing. It does not compare against plain, and it does not draw a screen in order to compare it. An implementation review without a screenshot or a URL writes nothing.

No screen is delivered without its states. On error, what the person typed is kept.

User flow, wireflow, and sitemap stay here. An activity diagram or a state machine is asked of `plugin-uml-diagrams`. The WCAG audit and the accessibility notes are asked of `plugin-accessibility`. Interface copy is asked of `plugin-ux-writing`. The use case is taken from `plugin-project-manager`. The test scenario stays in `plugin-qa-engineer`.

Do not write HTML or interface code.

Write the artifact in the language of the request. The type in the file name stays the English piece id.
